WHY THIS FILE EXISTS

Free software is rarely one person's work. A deployment of Nomen runs the
Program, the libraries it depends on, the plugins and skins its operator chose
to install, and the packages those bring with them. Each of them has authors,
and each carries a license of its own.

The Version Page is where a deployment names them. It lists the Program, the
plugins, the skins and the libraries, so that the people who wrote them are
acknowledged where their work actually runs. An attribution nobody can reach
credits nobody, which is why Section 2 asks for a link as well as the words,
and why Section 4 asks that the page stay public.

This is not a branding requirement. Nomen is free software: you may change it,
rename it and run it as you see fit. What these terms ask is that the chain of
credit survives being passed on, and that a deployment presenting itself as
Nomen keeps the page that says whose work it is. Section 6 provides the other
way out: rebrand, and the deployment no longer relies on the permission granted
there. Section 2 continues to apply whenever the Program itself is conveyed.

The GPL's own preamble makes the same argument at greater length.


